        "block-2": {
          "type": "content_block",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Cleaning Methods for Different Types of Jewellery",
            "body": "<p><strong>Gold Jewellery:</strong> Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water. Soak the piece for 10–15 minutes, gently brush with a soft-bristled toothbrush, rinse thoroughly and dry with a soft, lint-free cloth.</p><p><strong>Silver Jewellery:</strong> Use a silver polishing cloth for light tarnish. For heavier tarnish, use a silver cleaner according to the product instructions, then rinse thoroughly and dry completely.</p><p><strong>Platinum Jewellery:</strong> Soak in mild soap and warm water for about 5 minutes, gently brush with a soft toothbrush, rinse well and dry with a soft cloth.</p>",
            "callout": true,
            "list_heading": "",
            "list_items": "",
            "list_style": "bullet",
            "image_1_alt": "Silver ring showing metal care and polishing needs",
            "image_1_fallback": "silver-ring-care.webp",
            "image_2_alt": "",
            "image_2_fallback": "",
            "cta_text": "",
            "cta_link": ""
          }
        },
        "block-3": {
          "type": "content_block",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Gemstone Jewellery",
            "body": "<p>Different gemstones require different care. Diamonds can be cleaned with a solution of ammonia and water, while sapphires and rubies can be cleaned similarly. Softer stones such as emeralds and opals should only be cleaned with a damp, soft cloth. Avoid soaking delicate gemstones or using ultrasonic cleaners without professional advice.</p>",
            "callout": false,
            "list_heading": "",
            "list_items": "",
            "list_style": "bullet",
            "image_1_alt": "Opal vintage gold ring requiring careful gemstone care",
            "image_1_fallback": "opal-vintage-gold-ring.webp",
            "image_2_alt": "",
            "image_2_fallback": "",
            "cta_text": "Book an appointment",
            "cta_link": "/pages/booking"
          }
        },
        "block-4": {
          "type": "content_block",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Storage Tips to Prevent Damage and Tarnishing",
            "body": "",
            "callout": false,
            "list_heading": "",
            "list_items": "Keep pieces separate in soft pouches or a jewellery box with separate compartments.\nStore jewellery in a cool, dry place to reduce tarnishing.\nUse silica gel packets to absorb moisture.\nHang necklaces to prevent tangling.\nStore silver pieces in airtight bags to reduce tarnishing.",
            "list_style": "bullet",
            "image_1_alt": "Single diamond ring stored safely in a light jewellery box",
            "image_1_fallback": "single-diamond-ring-box.webp",
            "image_2_alt": "Diamond halo stud earrings stored separately on satin",
            "image_2_fallback": "diamond-halo-stud-earrings.webp",
            "cta_text": "",
            "cta_link": ""
          }
        },
        "block-5": {
          "type": "content_block",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "When to Seek Professional Cleaning Services",
            "body": "<p>Professional cleaning should be part of your jewellery care routine, especially for frequently worn pieces, antique pieces, valuable items, or any jewellery showing signs of damage or loose stones.</p>",
            "callout": false,
            "list_heading": "Common Jewellery Care Mistakes to Avoid",
            "list_items": "Wearing jewellery during heavy physical activity\nExposing jewellery to chlorine, swimming pools, lotions or household cleaners\nUsing abrasive or harsh chemical cleaners\nNeglecting professional inspections\nStoring different pieces together without protection",
            "list_style": "bullet",
            "image_1_alt": "Sapphire and diamond halo earrings for professional jewellery inspection",
            "image_1_fallback": "sapphire-diamond-halo-earrings.webp",
            "image_2_alt": "",
            "image_2_fallback": "",
            "cta_text": "",
            "cta_link": ""
          }
        },
        "block-6": {
          "type": "content_block",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Maintenance Schedule for Different Types of Jewellery",
            "body": "<p><strong>Daily:</strong> Wipe jewellery with a soft cloth after wearing.</p><p><strong>Weekly:</strong> Give frequently worn pieces a gentle clean with mild soap and water.</p><p><strong>Monthly:</strong> Check for signs of damage, loose stones, worn claws or damaged clasps.</p><p><strong>Bi-annually:</strong> Have valuable or frequently worn pieces professionally cleaned and checked.</p><p><strong>Annually:</strong> Schedule a professional cleaning and inspection for all fine jewellery.</p>",
            "callout": true,
